      "translation": "The ocean appears blue primarily due to the way water interacts with sunlight. Sunlight is composed of all colors of the visible spectrum. When this light enters water, the water molecules preferentially absorb the longer wavelengths (red, orange, yellow). The shorter, higher-energy wavelengths, particularly blue, are scattered in all directions by the water molecules. This phenomenon, known as Rayleigh scattering, causes the blue light to be reflected back to our eyes from all depths, making the vast expanse of the ocean appear blue. The clarity and depth of the water influence the intensity of this blue hue.",
